---A PrivateLink endpoint, which connects a project to an AWS VPC endpoint service in a single region so that traffic reaches the service over AWS PrivateLink rather than the public internet.
---@class vercel.networking.PrivateLinkEndpoint
---@field awsDnsEntries? vercel.networking.PrivateLinkEndpointAwsDnsEntriesList The regional DNS names assigned to the endpoint by AWS. Use these to reach the service when private DNS is not enabled.
---@field awsServiceName string The AWS VPC endpoint service the endpoint connects to.
---@field createdAt number Timestamp in milliseconds since the UNIX epoch for when the endpoint was created.
---@field endpointId string The unique identifier of the PrivateLink endpoint.
---@field name string The name of the PrivateLink endpoint, shown in the Vercel dashboard.
---@field privateDnsNames? vercel.networking.PrivateLinkEndpointPrivateDnsNamesList The private DNS names of the endpoint service, populated when private DNS is enabled for the endpoint.
---@field projectId string The identifier of the project the PrivateLink endpoint belongs to.
---@field status vercel.networking.PrivateLinkEndpointStatus The current state of the endpoint. - `creating`: the endpoint is being created. - `pending-acceptance`: waiting for the endpoint service owner to accept the connection. Only occurs for services that require manual acceptance. - `provisioning`: the connection was accepted and AWS is finishing setup. - `available`: the endpoint is fully provisioned and ready to use. - `rejected`: the endpoint service owner rejected the connection. - `failed`: the endpoint could not be provisioned. - `deleting`: the endpoint is being deleted.
---@field statusMessage? string A human-readable explanation of why the endpoint could not be provisioned. Only set when `status` is `failed`, and absent for every other status including `rejected`, since AWS does not report a rejection reason.
---@field teamId string The identifier of the team that owns the PrivateLink endpoint.
---@field updatedAt number Timestamp in milliseconds since the UNIX epoch for when the endpoint was last updated.
---@field vercelRegion string The Vercel region the endpoint is provisioned in.
---@field vpcEndpointId? string The identifier of the underlying AWS VPC endpoint. Absent until AWS has created the endpoint.

---The regional DNS names assigned to the endpoint by AWS. Use these to reach the service when private DNS is not enabled.
---@alias vercel.networking.PrivateLinkEndpointAwsDnsEntriesList string[]

---The private DNS names of the endpoint service, populated when private DNS is enabled for the endpoint.
